# Vitest suites live next to the routes they cover. That is a deliberate
# repository convention — but Vercel treats every non-underscore `.ts` file
# under `api/` as a Serverless Function entrypoint, so five test files were
# being deployed as functions: they occupied five of the twelve a Hobby
# deployment may have, and answered nothing (no default handler) if anyone
# called them.
#
# That left the project sitting at exactly the limit, so #181's `api/mcp.ts`
# failed the whole deployment with `exceeded_serverless_functions_per_deployment`
# rather than anything wrong with the route. Excluding the suites takes the
# real count to eight and leaves room to add routes again.
#
# `npm run check` and CI still type-check and run every one of these; nothing
# about the tests changes except that they stop being deployed.
api/**/*.test.ts
